  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale  \n   The Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem requires finding a step function that minimizes the maximum correlation with its shift. Existing methods focus on binary representations and local smoothing, which can struggle with complex structures. Our approach combines continuous optimization with dynamic neighborhood exploration to find spatially structured solutions. The key idea is to:  \n   - Use continuous optimization to escape local optima  \n   - Employ a two-phase process (initial annealing followed by structured refinement)  \n   - Explore diverse structural patterns through adaptive penalty functions  \n   This method addresses the bottleneck of local search by introducing correlation-driven pattern formation, mimicking how natural systems form organized structures under constraints.  \n   \n   Bottlenecks addressed:  \n   1. Local search limitations - enhanced by adaptive exploration  \n   2. Binary-reliance constraint - maintains continuous flexibility  \n   3. Suboptimal gradient handling - improved derivative estimation  \n\n2. Mathematical specification  \n   Representation: Four samples across [0,2] grid, defined as vector `x \u2208 \u211d^4 \\ [0,1]` with `sum(x) = 2`  \n   Objective: Minimize `C(x) = max_k \u211d_{kernel}(x) dx` where `dx = 0.5`  \n   Constraints: `0 \u2264 x_i \u2264 1` \u2200i, `\u2211x_i = 2`  \n   Adjustable parameters:  \n     `\u03bc` - Diversity penalty coefficient (default 200)  \n     `\u03bd` - Structural complexity modifier (default 10)  \n     `\u03bb` - Refined neighborhood radius (default 1)  \n\n   Key variables:  \n     `K = [0,1,2,3]` - Spatial indices  \n     `\u03c8(x) = max_k |\u03a3x_j\u03b8(j-k)|` - Extended correlation function  \n     `g(x) = \u03bc(|x_i - 0.5|) + \u03bd(D(x))` - Structure penalty  \n   Optimization domain: Composite objective `\u03c6(x) = max(\u03c8(x), g(x))`  \n\n3. Implementation procedure  \n   a. Initialization  \n      i. Start from feasible point via random walk with cooling factor `\u03b1=0.95`  \n      ii. Transform parent using `C(x_parent) \u2192 x_child = f(x_parent)`  \n      iii. Apply initial projection: `x_clip = project_feasible(x, 4)`  \n\n   b. Optimization loop  \n      i. Adaptive neighborhood construction:  \n          - Sample `6\u03bd` random points in parameter space  \n          - Resize local region around best solution `x_best`  \n      ii. Quasi-gradient step:  \n          - Estimate `\u2207\u03c6(x) \u2248 (\u03c6(x+\u03b5)-\u03c6(x))/\u03b5`  \n          - Take step: `x_new = x_project(np.clip(x_best+\u03b7\u2207\u03c6, 0, 1))`  \n      iii. Post-optimal restructuring:  \n          - `(\u03c8,D)=(estimate_structure(x_best),1)`  \n          - Solve auxiliary optimization `min_x \u03c6(x)` over `||x-x_best||<\u03bb`  \n\n   c. Terminal conditions  \n      - Max epochs: 1000 (with checkpoint at 500)  \n      - Success if `\u03c6(x_new) < \u03c4` or stall detected (`100` iterations without improvement)  \n\n4. Search choices  \n   Default configuration:  \n     `\u03bc=200, \u03bd=10, \u03bb=1`  \n     - Nationally scaled weight adjustment: `if|\u03c6_prev-\u03c6_new|<1e-4\u03bc+=10`  \n     - Random mutation with history-based probability  \n   Varied versions:  \n     - Representation-vary: Three-grid `n=4,n=8,n=12` comparison  \n     - Objective-vary: Absolute vs. relative correlation measure  \n\n5. Budget allocation  \n   - Core optimization: 1000 steps, O(4\u2207\u03c6/step)  \n   - Feasibility check: O(4projection)  \n   - Stopping check: `if time() > t0+1100` break  \n   - Estimated total time: ~800s  \n\n6. Validity checks  \n   - Force feasible via `x_clip = np.clip(x,0,1); x_project = clip+scale*(sum(x_clip)-sum(x))`  \n   - Re-evaluate via `cross_check = np.mean([\u03c6(x_roll)%10 for x_roll in[x+(-0.5)]])`  \n   - Measurement penalty on numerical instability  \n   Serve fallback: `return(np.array([0.5,0.5,0,0])).astype(float), compute_c5(h,4),4`  \n   Final code block must include all helper functions and meet the runtime limit",
